mistake.  It was a bit unfortunate but here's what you *could* have done.

Wait in the sokoban L1 for 600 turns (without a luck stone in your
inventory).  If your luck was -1, that should have moved the luck back to 0.
Make sure you were in a safe corner with all of your pets nearby.  If you
have the resource, Engrave Elbereth and levitate over for the duration.

If you think you were further negative into the luck problem.  Wait longer.
If you have resource, you could have also used Enlightenment or some such to
actually figure out if/when it's safe to pray.

When you first saw the pony, you should have tried immediately to
tame/pacify.  In general, domestic animals are *far* more dangerous when
they start to show up relative to the other monsters you can encounter.
Throw a vegetable based food (Lichen corpses last forever just so you know.
I don't even eat'em until I have to and I just carry them around just for
horses) and they'll be tame.  I think if you throw *any* food they'll be
pacified.  I don't know if that was an option before you got confused, but
if those were options, that should have been your first action.

I agree that once you got confused, you were kind of screwed.  I am assuming
here you didn't have resources to handle being confused (unihorn, various
healing potions, maybe scroll of scare monster?, aforementioned teleport
scrolls etcs).

I think the key was to get rid of that negative luck before you left sokoban
